    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **52 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist rule in the owner-create flow.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.normalizeEmail(...)` (the method that handles `POST /api/owners`):\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n- After the existing syntax validation, the email's domain (the part after `@`, compared case-insensitively against the normalized/lower-cased value) is checked against the blocklist. A match throws `InvalidEmailException`.\n- Added the `java.util.Set` import.\n\n**Why reuse `InvalidEmailException`:** it already maps to **400 Bad Request** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice` with an `errors: [\"email\"]` body, matching the spec's \"reject with 400\" requirement and keeping the change idiomatic \u2014 a disposable domain is just another form of an unacceptable email. The check runs before the value is written back, so a rejected create never persists.\n\nThe new acceptance test `Cp38Tests.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
